The GPU to GPU demo, on the machine's GPU. Two nodes' lines interleave
as they happen, so each node's are checked in order after a stable sort.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: %libomp-env make -s -C %S/../../examples run-gpu-to-gpu MERKC=merkc BUILD=%t O=2 PORT=47102 ARCH=%offload-arch "LIBOMP_FLAGS=%libomp-flags" | grep "^.[nG]" | sort -s -k1,2 | FileCheck %s --match-full-lines

CHECK:[GPU A] sending numbers, each 1
CHECK-NEXT:[GPU A] got the sum 1000
CHECK-NEXT:[GPU A] sending numbers, each 2
CHECK-NEXT:[GPU A] got the sum 2000
CHECK-NEXT:[GPU A] sending numbers, each 3
CHECK-NEXT:[GPU A] got the sum 3000
CHECK-NEXT:[GPU B] got this many numbers: 1000
CHECK-NEXT:[GPU B] sending back their sum 1000
CHECK-NEXT:[GPU B] got this many numbers: 1000
CHECK-NEXT:[GPU B] sending back their sum 2000
CHECK-NEXT:[GPU B] got this many numbers: 1000
CHECK-NEXT:[GPU B] sending back their sum 3000
CHECK-NEXT:[node A] connecting to node B at 127.0.0.1:{{[0-9]+}}
CHECK-NEXT:[node A] found node B's mailboxes
CHECK-NEXT:[node A] round 1
CHECK-NEXT:[node A] round 2
CHECK-NEXT:[node A] round 3
CHECK-NEXT:[node B] listening on port {{[0-9]+}}
CHECK-NEXT:[node B] node A has connected
CHECK-NEXT:[node B] round 1
CHECK-NEXT:[node B] round 2
CHECK-NEXT:[node B] round 3
